 **Can the six Voyages without a BOOST value pay for BOOST?** No. They have **no BOOST value**, rather than a printed zero, and cannot be discarded as BOOST payment. **Voyage Home is the exception: it has BOOST 1.** The original components identify these cards. Designer/publisher Justin Jacobson’s [October 17, 2019 explanation](https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2294803/any-rule-of-thumb-for-boost-values) confirms that the omissions intentionally prevent Sinbad from dumping Voyages into his discard pile this way. This original-fighter clarification does not introduce other sets’ rules.
 
-**Original Excalibur versus Feint ruling:** even though Excalibur has no printed effect, Feint cancels Arthur’s ability BOOST; discard the BOOST card without effect and retain Excalibur’s printed attack value 6. Designer Justin Jacobson [expressly confirmed that original intent on January 2, 2021](https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2455319/article/36640902#36640902). A screenshot circulated in 2025 reports replacing this ruling for later competitive and organized play. Its specific publisher authorship could not be independently authenticated in this run, so that replacement is not adopted here. This page’s original-rule ruling should not be taken as confirmation of current tournament policy.
+**Excalibur versus Feint — official August 11, 2025 erratum:** IELLO [published the official Restoration Games change](https://iello.fr/unmatched-inarretable-excalibur/) for both casual play and tournaments. Textless Excalibur has no printed effect that Feint can cancel, so Arthur’s ability BOOST still applies. Excalibur’s printed attack value remains 6 before adding that BOOST. This exception does not preserve BOOST on another Arthur card whose effects actually are canceled. Resolve ordinary combat damage, then discard played cards normally; the cancellation does not return the BOOST card to hand.
+
+**Historical reference, superseded August 2025:** the original interpretation removed the ability BOOST even from Excalibur against Feint. Designer Justin Jacobson [confirmed that prior intent on January 2, 2021](https://boardgamegeek.com/thread/2455319/article/36640902#36640902). Under that historical interpretation only, Excalibur retained value 6 after cancellation. The publisher’s 2025 erratum replaces this historical ruling for current play.
